    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "This method is called after any attempt to seek or change the playback direction of the item’s content.",
      "ko": "When your app enters a state where using a video decoder resources is not permissible, the value of this property changes to [`true`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/true) along with the video renderer’s status changing to [`AVQueuedSampleBufferRenderingStatus.failed`](avqueuedsamplebufferrenderingstatus/failed.md).",
      "sourceHash": "f2cbab0e3e3c8a06f3d91c40d60a54499ac441e223081a78985a72291893670d",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "If you are maintaining any queued future samples, you can use your implementation of this method to discard those samples.",
      "ko": "To resume rendering sample buffers, you must first reset the video renderer by calling [`flush()`](avqueuedsamplebufferrendering/flush().md) or [`flush(removingDisplayedImage:completionHandler:)`](avsamplebuffervideorenderer/flush(removingdisplayedimage:completionhandler:).md).",
      "sourceHash": "f7770a70f6694ef1bfc8f258a2b3df0daf6402f328a76bda16527d4787f0cac7",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
